  "seoTitle": "Indonesian Police Fire Ahrie Sonta Over Wiretapping",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian National Police dismissed Irjen Ahrie Sonta following an ethics trial that found him guilty of illegally wiretapping President Prabowo.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Indonesian National Police dismissed Irjen Ahrie Sonta after an ethics committee found him guilty of unauthorized wiretapping.",
    "The investigation concluded that the former official committed professional misconduct regarding the surveillance of the President.",
    "Sonta has officially filed an appeal against the decision, while oversight bodies confirmed the trial followed proper legal procedures."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police (Polri) held a ten-hour ethics trial, resulting in the dishonorable discharge of Irjen Ahrie Sonta. The disciplinary committee found that Sonta engaged in illegal wiretapping activities targeting President Prabowo and other unidentified parties. The decision has drawn support from various public figures and oversight organizations, such as the National Police Commission (Kompolnas), which observed the proceedings to ensure procedural accountability. Academics have highlighted the incident as a significant national security issue, emphasizing the risks associated with the unauthorized surveillance of state leaders. Following the verdict, the police leadership reiterated a zero-tolerance policy regarding the abuse of official authority by personnel. Sonta, who previously served as the head of the police legal division, has formally initiated an appeal process to contest the ruling made by the Ethics Commission.",
